---
/*
 * The mark ("infinite loop"): a hand-drawn spiral, loose loops tightening into
 * a dense inner ring, rasterized onto a 40x40 pixel grid and glitched: a band
 * of rows torn sideways by uneven amounts, a smaller tear the other way, single
 * rows jittered, one scanline dropped, stray pixels off the edges. Each rect is
 * one run of pixels in one row. Shown at 120px, so each pixel is exactly 3px.
 * public/favicon.svg is a separate 16x16 drawing of the same loop.
 *
 * The g1/g2 rows are the tears that jump when the logo is hovered; the
 * animation lives in global.css under "logo glitch".
 */
